  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Points \\(A(-2,y_1)\\), \\(B(1,y_2)\\), and \\(C(3,y_3)\\) all lie on the line \\(y=-3x+1\\). The order of \\(y_1\\), \\(y_2\\), and \\(y_3\\) is ( ).",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(y_1<y_2<y_3\\)",
    "B": "\\(y_2>y_1>y_3\\)",
    "C": "\\(y_1>y_3>y_2\\)",
    "D": "\\(y_1>y_2>y_3\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Since \\(k=-3<0\\), \\(y\\) decreases as \\(x\\) increases. Also, \\(-2<1<3\\), so \\(y_1>y_2>y_3\\). Alternatively, substitution gives \\(y_1=7\\), \\(y_2=-2\\), and \\(y_3=-8\\).",
